-- Naming: "Book N" → "Part N" (module descriptions, lesson subtitles, course description).
update public.p2p_curriculums set description = $gs$Seven parts that walk from life before Christ to a lifetime of following Him: Pre-Salvation, Jesus Christ, The Gospel, Responding to the Gospel, Assurance of Salvation, Baptism and Identification With Christ, and From Convert to Disciple.$gs$
  where id = 'f6a2b3f6-b66d-45d6-8065-c46d7b63441b' and description like 'Seven books %';
update public.p2p_modules set description = $gs$Part 1 · Pre-Salvation — This part explains the human condition apart from Christ, God’s kindness and witness, why people cannot save themselves, and how believers can care for those who do not yet know Jesus.$gs$ where id = '4bd7c674-fdfd-5754-b553-7dcafca7a054' and description is distinct from $gs$Part 1 · Pre-Salvation — This part explains the human condition apart from Christ, God’s kindness and witness, why people cannot save themselves, and how believers can care for those who do not yet know Jesus.$gs$;
update public.p2p_lessons set subtitle = $gs$Part 1 · Lesson 1.1$gs$ where id = 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e' and subtitle is distinct from $gs$Part 1 · Lesson 1.1$gs$;
update public.p2p_lessons set subtitle = $gs$Part 1 · Lesson 1.2$gs$ where id = '8ab26caf-d774-51fe-9234-6c1bdc2e9756' and subtitle is distinct from $gs$Part 1 · Lesson 1.2$gs$;
update public.p2p_lessons set subtitle = $gs$Part 1 · Lesson 1.3$gs$ where id = '270606b7-1a42-5995-8d45-da2d9db31a4d' and subtitle is distinct from $gs$Part 1 · Lesson 1.3$gs$;

-- Book 1 · Lesson 1.1: Dead in Trespasses and Sins
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('fedffc0f-43b0-5abe-9dc0-8d527d34989f', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 1, 'teaching', $gs$About this part$gs$, $gs$This plan teaches believers to understand the genuine, biblical condition of every person before Christ — examining Scripture’s teaching regarding humanity’s lost state, God’s gracious pursuit of the lost through common grace and conviction, and practical wisdom for cultivating genuine, gospel-centered compassion toward those who do not yet know Christ.$gs$),
  ('495db5fd-7cac-5205-8e7f-00323fd5988b', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 2, 'teaching', $gs$Root Scripture$gs$, $gs$“And you He made alive, who were dead in trespasses and sins.” — Ephesians 2:1$gs$),
  ('665233a4-a57b-5eed-9a28-c62cd40cc032', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Lecture$gs$, $gs$Before any person can rightly appreciate the good news of the gospel, they must first understand the genuinely bad news it answers. Scripture’s honest diagnosis of the human condition apart from Christ is not merely that people are imperfect or in need of self-improvement, but that they are spiritually dead — separated from God, under His righteous judgment, and utterly unable to rescue themselves through effort, religion, or good behavior. Understanding this pre-salvation condition rightly is not meant to produce despair, but genuine clarity — clarity that makes the gospel’s actual rescue comprehensible and precious rather than a vague, sentimental offer. This plan explores what Scripture teaches about the lost condition, how God graciously pursues the lost even before conversion through common grace, creation’s testimony, and the Spirit’s conviction, why human effort alone can never close this gap, and how believers can cultivate genuine, patient compassion for those still in this condition throughout ongoing life and witness.$gs$),
  ('2d821fdb-6b66-5d18-bb07-74c8c977b856', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 6, 'teaching', $gs$Key Bible passage$gs$, $gs$Ephesians 2:1–10$gs$),
  ('b509cf1a-3478-547a-b36c-1d3fb7a128f0', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Definition: What does it mean to be spiritually dead?$gs$, $gs$Spiritual death means being separated from God because of sin. It does not mean that a person is physically dead or unable to think, make decisions, love others, or do good things. It describes the broken relationship with God caused by sin.$gs$),
  ('33653787-ac79-5d10-87f2-9ca1d4ffd900', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 8, 'teaching', $gs$Simple explanation$gs$, $gs$• The Bible teaches that all people have sinned.
• Sin damages our relationship with God and leaves us in need of His forgiveness and help.
• Human effort, religious activity, or good behaviour cannot by themselves erase sin or earn salvation.
• Ephesians 2 goes on to explain that God, because of His mercy and love, makes people alive with Christ.
• Salvation is therefore a gift of God's grace, received through faith—not something people can earn by their own works.$gs$),
  ('e7c5f12d-f5c0-561a-a356-ac4c3c5e1f8a', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 9, 'teaching', $gs$Why is this important?$gs$, $gs$If our problem were only that we sometimes behave badly, we might think we only need to improve our behaviour. The Bible describes a deeper problem: sin has separated us from God. We need His forgiveness and the new life He gives through Jesus Christ.$gs$),
  ('c70b5046-25c7-5102-83b1-2d25436a6d4e', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 10, 'teaching', $gs$Important things to understand$gs$, $gs$• Spiritual death is not the same as physical death.
• It does not mean that people are incapable of kindness or good actions.
• It does not mean every person behaves in exactly the same way.
• It means that every person needs God's saving grace because of sin.$gs$),
  ('f60bae3f-3a20-51a6-902b-fbd5ea66c365', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 11, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$Why does Paul’s specific description — genuine spiritual “death,” not merely weakness or sickness — reveal that the pre-salvation condition is far more serious than mere moral imperfection requiring gradual correction?

Paul’s specific description reveals a condition more serious than moral imperfection, since genuine death, not weakness, establishes this severe reality, meaning the pre-salvation condition represents actual spiritual death, not merely correctable weakness, but this passage’s specific language particularly requiring recognition of death’s total, comprehensive severity as the honest, biblical description of every person’s condition apart from Christ’s own, gracious intervention and regenerating work.$gs$),
  ('a5c5a239-095e-5577-8752-d4fd0107f06f', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 12, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$How does understanding this death as total, not partial, explain why no amount of human effort, willpower, or religious activity can produce spiritual life, since dead things cannot make themselves alive through their own, internal effort?

Understanding this death as total explains the insufficiency of human effort, since dead things cannot selfresurrect through internal effort, meaning no amount of willpower or religious activity can produce genuine spiritual life, but this passage’s honest description requiring recognition that only an external, divine act — not internal human striving — can genuinely address this condition of total spiritual death.$gs$),
  ('093d2adb-7556-5c33-8282-bbcf0d11b28f', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 13, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Describing this condition as spiritual death does not mean unbelievers are incapable of any genuine kindness, morality, or civic good; it means that, however genuinely good such actions may be, they cannot produce the spiritual life only God can grant.$gs$),
  ('964c08a8-4630-5164-b69c-2fb56544f350', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 15, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Ephesians 2:1-3 and reflect on the honest, comprehensive description of spiritual death.
2. Identify a specific way you have witnessed this condition, without judgment, in someone’s life.
3. Write a short paragraph describing your own, pre-salvation condition in this passage’s honest terms.
4. Discuss with your peer guide how understanding this diagnosis shaped their own gratitude for grace.
5. Pray specifically for someone you know who remains in this condition, asking God for their genuine rescue.$gs$),
  ('2f333858-bd5a-5928-8d64-dedbf848a8fe', 'c2c5f8e5-9d00-515b-a075-ec8060385a3e', 16, 'teaching', $gs$Practical application (sample lesson)$gs$, $gs$Read Ephesians 2:1–10. Write a short paragraph describing the difference between the condition people are in because of sin and the new life God offers through Christ.$gs$)
on conflict (id) do nothing;
