-- Book 1 · Lesson 4.3: A Lifetime of Gospel-Centered Compassion
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('9320c6a5-9fc9-5e87-a05b-f34993021fe4', '45802359-ee8b-5b2b-bf59-8a0ee3d30e73', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$What is the ultimate posture believers are meant to carry throughout their entire lives regarding this genuine understanding of humanity’s lost condition?

A sustained, lifelong commitment to understanding the genuine severity of the lost condition without despair, recognizing God’s gracious pursuit through common grace, general revelation, and the Spirit’s conviction, understanding why human effort alone can never provide rescue, and cultivating genuine, Christlike compassion — not obligation — for every person who remains in this condition throughout every season of ongoing life and witness.$gs$),
  ('730b2602-bcc5-5430-b717-6c588007e16d', '45802359-ee8b-5b2b-bf59-8a0ee3d30e73', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$Why must this understanding remain an ongoing, lifelong posture rather than doctrine learned once and then set aside without continued, compassionate application throughout believers’ daily life and relationship?

Because new people, in this same genuine condition, will continue crossing believers’ paths throughout every season of ongoing life, this understanding necessarily requires continued, compassionate application throughout an entire lifetime, not doctrine set aside once learned, but requiring this ongoing, genuine compassion and readiness throughout believers’ continued, daily witness and relationship with those still without Christ.$gs$),
  ('b8abf112-ad74-5740-9d99-693b56cc098b', '45802359-ee8b-5b2b-bf59-8a0ee3d30e73', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Carrying this lifelong posture does not mean every interaction becomes a forced evangelistic transaction; it means genuine, patient love that remains ready, in season and out, to speak the truth this entire plan has explored whenever the door genuinely opens.$gs$),
  ('20ced1be-ed59-5ea4-a050-af1966e92572', '45802359-ee8b-5b2b-bf59-8a0ee3d30e73', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Romans 1:14-16 once more, reflecting on Paul’s own, lifelong sense of debt and compassion.
2. Write a summary of the most important lesson you learned in this entire plan.
3. Identify one specific practice from this plan you will commit to as a lifelong habit.
4. Share your growth with your peer guide, along with continued areas for growth and prayer.
5. Write a closing prayer committing to a lifetime of gospel-centered compassion for the lost in every season ahead.$gs$)
