-- Book 2 · Lesson 1.1: Fully God, Fully Man
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('e3a815e5-54e0-57fc-a2f6-654e2c8e904f', '01980f6e-8cb0-5595-a343-5103d301ffb1', 1, 'teaching', $gs$About this part$gs$, $gs$This plan teaches believers to understand the genuine, biblical person and work of Jesus Christ — examining Scripture’s teaching regarding His full deity and full humanity, His atoning death and bodily resurrection, His titles and roles, and practical wisdom for worshiping and following Him wholly throughout ongoing faith and discipleship.$gs$),
  ('f8034a5a-b18e-571b-b059-18e3e08392af', '01980f6e-8cb0-5595-a343-5103d301ffb1', 2, 'teaching', $gs$Root Scripture$gs$, $gs$“Jesus said to him, ‘I am the way, the truth, and the life. No one comes to the Father except through Me.’” — John 14:6$gs$),
  ('7d76fdac-5cbe-5b2f-9b1e-bf6f76245840', '01980f6e-8cb0-5595-a343-5103d301ffb1', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Lecture$gs$, $gs$Every dimension of the Christian faith ultimately rests on who Jesus Christ actually is and what He actually accomplished. Scripture presents Him as no mere teacher or moral example, but the eternal Son of God who took on genuine humanity, lived a sinless life, died a substitutionary death for sin, rose bodily from the grave, ascended to the Father’s right hand, and now reigns as Lord over all creation. Understanding Christ rightly requires holding together truths that can feel paradoxical to human reason — fully God and fully man, humble servant and reigning King, crucified and risen — without diminishing either side of these genuine, biblical realities. This plan explores the person of Christ, the completed work of Christ, His various titles and roles throughout Scripture, and practical wisdom for responding to who He genuinely is through worship and wholehearted discipleship throughout ongoing faith and life.$gs$),
  ('d8c423dc-b22e-5e13-8cf4-c6ce6e460e2c', '01980f6e-8cb0-5595-a343-5103d301ffb1', 6, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$Why does John’s specific declaration — the eternal “Word” genuinely becoming “flesh” — reveal that Christ is authentically both fully God and fully man together, not merely appearing human while remaining only divine, nor a lesser being somewhere between the two?

John’s specific declaration reveals Christ as authentically both fully God and fully man, since the eternal Word genuinely becoming flesh establishes this dual, complete reality, meaning Christ is neither merely appearing human nor a lesser, intermediate being, but this passage’s specific declaration particularly requiring recognition of this genuine, dual nature as central, biblical truth regarding Christ’s actual, complete person throughout Scripture’s consistent testimony and the church’s historic confession.$gs$),
  ('b66e17b4-cb05-5924-a923-3af442030600', '01980f6e-8cb0-5595-a343-5103d301ffb1', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$How does holding both natures together — without diminishing either His genuine deity or His genuine humanity — provide the necessary foundation for understanding why Christ alone could accomplish the atonement Module 2 will explore, since only a genuinely human sacrifice could represent humanity, and only a genuinely divine sacrifice could satisfy infinite justice?

Holding both natures together provides necessary foundation for the atonement, since only genuine humanity can represent humanity while only genuine deity can satisfy infinite justice, meaning this dual nature is not abstract theological curiosity but the actual, necessary foundation for Christ’s atoning work, requiring both genuine humanity and genuine deity together as this passage’s declaration specifically establishes throughout Scripture’s teaching regarding Christ’s complete, necessary person.$gs$),
  ('6efdafa9-59d3-541e-9148-28f11a021d07', '01980f6e-8cb0-5595-a343-5103d301ffb1', 8, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Affirming both natures does not mean Christ was partly God and partly man, as though divided; historic Christian teaching affirms He is fully, completely both at once, two natures united in one person, a genuine mystery to be believed, not fully explained by human reason.$gs$),
  ('eaff5141-69da-5b3b-808e-68b757c9cdf4', '01980f6e-8cb0-5595-a343-5103d301ffb1', 10, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read John 1:1-14 and reflect on the eternal Word genuinely becoming flesh.
2. Identify one passage emphasizing Christ’s deity and one emphasizing His genuine humanity, and compare them.
3. Write a simple, two-sentence explanation of Christ’s dual nature you could share with someone else.
4. Discuss with your peer guide how they hold both truths together in their own understanding and worship.
5. Journal about your own worship deepening as you consider both Christ’s deity and humanity together.$gs$)
