-- Book 2 · Lesson 1.3: Christ’s Sinless Life
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('d9e9705b-c3c4-5e33-819f-38dbcd1b8181', '30e612e3-1277-56a2-b8c2-14355aea956b', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$Why does this passage’s specific qualifier — genuinely tempted “as we are,” yet “without sin” — reveal that Christ’s sinlessness was not merely theoretical or automatic, but genuinely tested and proven through real, human temptation and experience?

This passage’s specific qualifier reveals genuinely tested sinlessness, since tempted “as we are, yet without sin” establishes real, proven experience, meaning Christ’s sinlessness was not merely theoretical or automatic, but genuinely tested through real temptation, but this passage’s specific qualifier particularly requiring recognition of this proven, experienced sinlessness as characteristic of Christ’s genuine, complete human experience throughout His earthly life and ministry.$gs$),
  ('94f4ec33-4a96-5385-9abc-2ff123688423', '30e612e3-1277-56a2-b8c2-14355aea956b', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$How does this proven sinlessness qualify Christ uniquely to serve as the sacrifice Module 2 will explore, since only a genuinely sinless offering could atone for sin without also needing atonement for its own, personal guilt?

This proven sinlessness qualifies Christ uniquely as sacrifice, since a sinless offering, unlike any other, requires no atonement of its own, meaning Christ’s genuine, proven sinlessness is not incidental detail but this passage’s necessary qualification for His unique role as sacrifice, without which His death could not accomplish the atoning work this plan’s second module will specifically explore and explain throughout Scripture’s teaching.$gs$),
  ('5bf99354-8de9-5d02-8394-79eea3be742f', '30e612e3-1277-56a2-b8c2-14355aea956b', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Affirming Christ’s sinlessness does not mean His temptations were somehow unreal or less difficult than ours; Scripture presents His temptation as genuinely real and difficult, making His sinless response all the more remarkable, not less significant.$gs$),
  ('27da8b3c-11bd-5acf-9e1e-9a39a1dd7635', '30e612e3-1277-56a2-b8c2-14355aea956b', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Hebrews 4:14-16 and reflect on Christ’s genuinely tested, proven sinlessness.
2. Identify a current struggle where you could draw comfort from Christ’s genuine understanding.
3. Bring this specific struggle to God in prayer, drawing on this passage’s promise of sympathetic help.
4. Discuss with your peer guide how Christ’s proven sinlessness has shaped their own confidence in His sacrifice.
5. Journal about the comfort and confidence this truth provides for your own, ongoing struggle with temptation.$gs$)
