-- Book 2 · Lesson 2.3: His Ascension and Present Reign
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('b4e6a6e1-d148-550e-98ca-d91b4bd50ce5', '2630eddb-e2ea-5107-b631-1d9852e639ad', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$Why does this passage’s specific description — Christ genuinely “received up” and now seated at God’s “right hand” — reveal that His work did not conclude with the resurrection, but continues in His present, active reign and ongoing ministry?

This passage’s specific description reveals continued, ongoing work, since being genuinely received up and seated establishes present, active reign, meaning Christ’s work did not conclude at the resurrection, but this passage’s specific description particularly requiring recognition of His present, active reign and continued ministry — including His ongoing intercession — as characteristic of Christ’s genuine, present position throughout believers’ understanding of His complete, comprehensive work.$gs$),
  ('65704df1-6afb-5260-8c8c-ac2e88e878b5', '2630eddb-e2ea-5107-b631-1d9852e639ad', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$How does understanding Christ’s present, active reign — not mere absence or distance — provide genuine comfort and confidence for believers navigating present, ongoing difficulty, since this passage reveals He is genuinely, actively reigning, not merely remembered from a completed, past story?

Understanding Christ’s present, active reign provides genuine comfort, since present, active reign differs from mere absence or distant memory, meaning believers navigating present difficulty should draw on this passage’s revelation of genuine, ongoing reign, not treating Christ as merely a past, completed story, but recognizing His present, active involvement throughout their ongoing life and continued relationship with Him.$gs$),
  ('faee3ea0-0866-5a58-87f7-632834d1e241', '2630eddb-e2ea-5107-b631-1d9852e639ad', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Affirming Christ’s present reign does not mean His physical absence is unimportant or without genuine significance; His bodily ascension establishes genuine, physical absence from earth even while His authority and active involvement remain genuinely, presently active through the Holy Spirit and His ongoing intercession.$gs$),
  ('1d264fbf-9575-5f15-bcb9-3d69a265ab36', '2630eddb-e2ea-5107-b631-1d9852e639ad', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Mark 16:19-20 and Hebrews 7:25 and reflect on Christ’s present, active reign and intercession.
2. Identify a current difficulty where you could draw comfort from Christ’s genuine, present involvement.
3. Pray specifically, acknowledging Christ’s active, ongoing reign in this particular circumstance.
4. Discuss with your peer guide how they draw comfort from Christ’s present reign in their own life.
5. Journal about your own, growing confidence in Christ’s active, ongoing presence and reign.$gs$)
