-- Book 2 · Lesson 3.2: Christ as Lord
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('83abc0b7-dfca-58e7-92c4-26d7aa253717', '0ea06a78-6bdf-5677-b338-bb9cadee2a62', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$Why does Paul’s specific pairing — confessing Jesus as “Lord,” alongside genuine belief — reveal that genuine faith includes submission to Christ’s actual authority, not remaining confined to intellectual agreement alone without this genuine, submitted allegiance?

Paul’s specific pairing reveals faith’s inclusion of submission, since confessing “Lord” alongside belief establishes this necessary allegiance, meaning genuine faith includes this submission to Christ’s actual authority, not remaining confined to intellectual agreement alone, but this passage’s specific pairing particularly requiring recognition of “Lord” as necessary confession alongside belief, characteristic of genuine, complete, saving faith throughout Scripture’s teaching regarding authentic conversion and continued discipleship.$gs$),
  ('cc7c05e4-3ddc-5ee5-a799-57b13363d775', '0ea06a78-6bdf-5677-b338-bb9cadee2a62', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$How does acknowledging Christ as Lord require ongoing, practical surrender of specific areas of life — finances, relationships, ambition — rather than a one-time, verbal confession disconnected from actual, continued obedience and submission?

Acknowledging Christ as Lord requires ongoing, practical surrender, since actual obedience differs from disconnected verbal confession, meaning believers should pursue this ongoing, practical surrender of specific life areas, not remaining confined to one-time confession alone, but embracing this passage’s called-for lordship as requiring genuine, continued obedience throughout their ongoing, daily life and relationship with Christ as genuine Lord, not merely acknowledged Savior.$gs$),
  ('cc27d50d-2fc6-5e93-8d84-771a91974cc3', '0ea06a78-6bdf-5677-b338-bb9cadee2a62', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Acknowledging Christ’s lordship does not mean achieving perfect, immediate obedience in every area; it means a genuine, ongoing posture of submission and growth, even amid continued struggle and incomplete surrender in specific areas still being worked out.$gs$),
  ('e602aa0f-c506-52cb-923e-419c4d15fbf5', '0ea06a78-6bdf-5677-b338-bb9cadee2a62', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Romans 10:9-10 and reflect on confessing Christ as Lord alongside genuine belief.
2. Identify one specific area of your life requiring greater, practical surrender to Christ’s lordship.
3. Take one concrete step of surrender in this specific area this week.
4. Discuss with your peer guide how they have grown in surrendering specific areas to Christ’s lordship over time.
5. Journal about your own, ongoing journey of surrender as you continue growing under Christ’s genuine lordship.$gs$)
