-- Book 2 · Lesson 3.3: Christ as the Coming King
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('bcf0152d-8b50-53c8-832a-aeb75efe0a99', 'fca33890-1adc-585c-8875-b15c6761b0a2', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$Why does John’s specific promise — Christ genuinely returning, visible to “every eye” — reveal that His current, hidden reign will one day give way to genuinely visible, universal recognition of His kingship over all creation?

John’s specific promise reveals a future, visible transition, since Christ’s return being visible to “every eye” establishes this genuine, universal recognition, meaning His current, hidden reign will one day become visible and universally acknowledged, but this passage’s specific promise particularly requiring recognition of this coming, visible reality as characteristic of believers’ genuine, biblical hope regarding Christ’s promised, future return and comprehensive reign over all creation.$gs$),
  ('390b18b7-c570-5b38-af34-324c4d7765e6', 'fca33890-1adc-585c-8875-b15c6761b0a2', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$How does this future hope shape believers’ present life, providing genuine motivation for faithful endurance and holy living now, since present circumstances, however difficult, are genuinely temporary compared to this passage’s promised, coming reality?

This future hope shapes present life, since temporary present circumstances differ from this promised, coming reality, meaning believers should draw genuine motivation from this future hope, enduring faithfully and living in holiness now, not remaining discouraged by present, temporary circumstance, but anchoring their present life in this passage’s promised, coming reality throughout their ongoing faith and continued, faithful endurance.$gs$),
  ('6fe519e8-f4b3-5f6c-b32d-3aad1062c44e', 'fca33890-1adc-585c-8875-b15c6761b0a2', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Anticipating Christ’s coming reign does not mean withdrawing from present, faithful engagement with the world; genuine hope in His return should motivate greater, not lesser, faithfulness in present responsibility and witness.$gs$),
  ('4bd3d15a-38da-55ea-b1e9-45bb1ff6eb14', 'fca33890-1adc-585c-8875-b15c6761b0a2', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Revelation 1:7 and Titus 2:11-13 and reflect on the promised, coming return of Christ as King.
2. Identify a current difficulty where this future hope could provide genuine motivation for faithful endurance.
3. Reflect on how this hope should shape greater present engagement, not withdrawal, from your responsibilities.
4. Discuss with your peer guide how anticipating Christ’s return shapes their own present faithfulness.
5. Journal about your own hope and motivation, anchored in Christ’s promised, coming reign over all creation.$gs$)
