-- Book 2 · Lesson 4.1: Worshiping Christ Rightly
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('a51de64b-f467-5450-9f82-6f895187bf7f', 'ceafd5e0-5294-5176-ba5f-8f63e98bf7b5', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$Why does this passage’s comprehensive declaration — Christ genuinely “worthy” of power, riches, wisdom, and glory — reveal that worship is the appropriate, comprehensive response to everything this plan has explored regarding His person and completed work?

This passage’s comprehensive declaration reveals worship as the appropriate, comprehensive response, since Christ’s genuine worthiness across every category establishes this fitting response, meaning worship represents the appropriate, comprehensive response to His person and work, not remaining confined to merely intellectual assent, but this passage’s comprehensive declaration particularly requiring genuine, comprehensive worship as characteristic of appropriate response throughout believers’ ongoing relationship with Christ and understanding of His genuine worth.$gs$),
  ('9ff59486-3c67-59d0-a5d7-c2273b96c43d', 'ceafd5e0-5294-5176-ba5f-8f63e98bf7b5', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$How does genuine worship require both understanding — the theological content this plan has explored — and heartfelt response, since worship divorced from genuine understanding becomes empty emotion, while understanding divorced from genuine response remains incomplete, cold theology?

Genuine worship requires both understanding and heartfelt response, since worship without understanding becomes empty emotion while understanding without response remains cold theology, meaning believers should hold both dimensions together, not settling for either alone, but pursuing this passage’s comprehensive, both intellectually grounded and genuinely felt worship throughout their ongoing relationship with and response to Christ’s genuine person and worth.$gs$),
  ('07e4f784-cbb7-5895-9550-f2eb11cc48e5', 'ceafd5e0-5294-5176-ba5f-8f63e98bf7b5', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Worshiping Christ rightly does not require identical, uniform emotional experience in every moment; genuine worship includes both seasons of strong feeling and seasons of quiet, faithful acknowledgment of truth, both genuinely valid expressions of the same, underlying worship.$gs$),
  ('9829dc4d-341f-564a-a0ed-372ebdcf6e73', 'ceafd5e0-5294-5176-ba5f-8f63e98bf7b5', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Revelation 5:9-13 and reflect on the comprehensive worship Christ’s worth genuinely deserves.
2. Identify the specific truth from this plan that has most moved you toward genuine worship.
3. Spend intentional time this week worshiping Christ, combining understanding with genuine, felt response.
4. Discuss with your peer guide how their understanding of Christ has deepened their own, genuine worship.
5. Journal about your own growth in worshiping Christ both rightly understood and genuinely felt.$gs$)
