-- Book 2 · Lesson 4.3: A Lifetime of Knowing Christ
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('1609ce2b-d75c-524e-90e4-4c5255470ec3', 'f3bd9cc6-f59f-5572-9b2f-9c8140e33314', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$What is the ultimate posture believers are meant to carry throughout their entire lives regarding this significant, comprehensive understanding of who Jesus Christ actually is?

A sustained, lifelong commitment to knowing Christ ever more deeply — His full deity and humanity, His completed, atoning work, His present reign, and His promised return — responding with genuine worship and wholehearted, costly following throughout every season of ongoing faith, understanding, and discipleship.$gs$),
  ('6c613a3a-95d5-5d00-8478-2875e6dbd772', 'f3bd9cc6-f59f-5572-9b2f-9c8140e33314', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$Why must this understanding remain an ongoing, lifelong pursuit rather than truth learned once and then set aside without continued, growing knowledge of Christ throughout believers’ ongoing spiritual life?

Because Christ’s own, infinite person and work continue providing genuine depth for growing knowledge throughout every season of ongoing life, this understanding necessarily requires continued, deliberate pursuit throughout an entire lifetime, not truth learned once and then set aside, but requiring this ongoing, deepening knowledge and worship throughout believers’ entire, continuing life and relationship with Christ.$gs$),
  ('0a734f2c-bb59-54ff-a24b-01ab3d48e8fd', 'f3bd9cc6-f59f-5572-9b2f-9c8140e33314', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Committing to this lifelong pursuit does not mean arriving at complete, exhaustive knowledge of Christ in this present life; the lifelong journey includes continued growth and discovery, with sustained, faithful pursuit of everdeepening knowledge being the genuine, ongoing goal.$gs$),
  ('eeea9f80-18c6-5726-8bd3-f112149d3b94', 'f3bd9cc6-f59f-5572-9b2f-9c8140e33314', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Philippians 3:7-10 once more, reflecting on the surpassing worth of genuinely knowing Christ.
2. Write a summary of the most important lesson you learned in this entire plan.
3. Identify one specific practice from this plan you will commit to as a lifelong habit.
4. Share your growth with your peer guide, along with continued areas for growth and deeper knowledge.
5. Write a closing prayer committing to a lifetime of ever-deepening knowledge of and devotion to Jesus Christ.$gs$)
on conflict (id) do nothing;
