  ('fe0fc9d5-56e1-56ae-b0e2-cc0a8562a349', 'd6f733d3-6d15-5591-ad2b-9364534ec539', 'paragraph', $gs${"text":"About this module\n\nThe gospel is the good news of what God has done through Jesus Christ to save sinners. The previous module explained the bad news: every person has sinned, every person stands accountable before God, and no person can rescue themselves through their own efforts. This module now turns to the good news that answers that problem.\n\nGod did not leave humanity without hope. In His love and mercy, He sent His Son, Jesus Christ, into the world. Jesus lived the perfect life that we have failed to live. He willingly gave His life on the cross, taking the punishment that sinners deserve. He was buried, and on the third day He rose bodily from the dead.\n\nHis death and resurrection are not simply events from history. They are the foundation of salvation. Through Christ, God offers forgiveness, peace with Himself, a new standing before Him, and eternal life. These blessings are not earned through good behaviour, religious activities, or personal achievement. They are received by grace through faith in Jesus Christ.\n\nThis module will help learners understand why Jesus had to die, what His resurrection accomplished, and why salvation is a gift that cannot be earned. The aim is not merely to know the facts of the gospel but to understand and trust the Saviour at the centre of it."}$gs$::jsonb, 1, false, false),
