-- Book 4 · Lesson 4.3: A Lifetime of Ongoing Response
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('2621fee4-ff0f-5dcb-90a8-0908e66509c7', 'd77baf10-0a2c-5c82-bebf-b2d4e7011b18', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$What is the ultimate posture believers are meant to carry throughout their entire lives regarding this significant, ongoing response to the gospel?

A sustained, lifelong commitment to genuine repentance and faith — turning from sin, trusting Christ alone, confessing Him openly, surrendering control, and continuing to respond honestly, not treating this response as a single, completed transaction, but as ongoing, daily posture throughout every season of continued life and relationship with Christ.$gs$),
  ('187397ac-3dba-568f-a7fc-31ce927c4ae5', 'd77baf10-0a2c-5c82-bebf-b2d4e7011b18', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$Why must this response remain an ongoing, lifelong posture rather than a single transaction completed once and then set aside without continued, daily application throughout believers’ ongoing spiritual life?

Because genuine repentance and faith require continued, daily expression throughout every season of ongoing life, not remaining a single, completed transaction, this response necessarily requires continued, deliberate practice throughout an entire lifetime, not truth applied once and then set aside, but requiring this ongoing, daily posture throughout believers’ entire, continuing relationship with Christ.$gs$),
  ('7285d29d-d669-52fc-8701-be2eb1b7a67d', 'd77baf10-0a2c-5c82-bebf-b2d4e7011b18', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Committing to this lifelong posture does not mean doubting the genuine reality of an initial, past decision; it means understanding that genuine faith continues expressing itself through ongoing repentance and trust throughout the remainder of a believer’s continuing life.$gs$),
  ('c9365ef7-6e15-5338-bdc3-28ea36cbd96b', 'd77baf10-0a2c-5c82-bebf-b2d4e7011b18', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Mark 1:14-15 once more, reflecting on the ongoing call to repent and believe.
2. Write a summary of the most important lesson you learned in this entire plan.
3. Identify one specific practice from this plan you will commit to as a lifelong habit.
4. Share your growth with your peer guide, along with continued areas for growth and response.
5. Write a closing prayer committing to a lifetime of genuine, ongoing repentance and faith in every season ahead.$gs$)
