-- Book 5 · Lesson 4.3: A Lifetime of Settled Confidence
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('ecbdfd56-154d-5247-a489-8cefa2bc1093', '9328d66a-ad45-5237-8437-e4a74d1006c2', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$What is the ultimate posture believers are meant to carry throughout their entire lives regarding this significant, biblical understanding of assurance?

A sustained, lifelong commitment to grounding assurance in God’s promise and Christ’s finished work, recognizing genuine evidences without confusing them with the primary foundation, navigating doubt and comparison with honest wisdom, and resting in grace throughout every season of ongoing spiritual life and continued relationship with God.$gs$),
  ('e56493f6-b6f9-5986-8525-bded1efb61df', '9328d66a-ad45-5237-8437-e4a74d1006c2', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$Why must this settled confidence remain an ongoing, lifelong posture rather than truth established once and then assumed without continued, sustained application throughout believers’ ongoing spiritual journey?

Because new seasons of doubt, comparison, and struggle will continue arising throughout every stage of ongoing life, this settled confidence necessarily requires continued, deliberate grounding throughout an entire lifetime, not truth established once and then assumed, but requiring this ongoing, intentional practice throughout believers’ entire, continuing relationship with God and understanding of their own, secure salvation.$gs$),
  ('1c9997f6-8d2d-5914-b19f-d6d0068368d0', '9328d66a-ad45-5237-8437-e4a74d1006c2', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Committing to this lifelong posture does not mean doubt will never again arise; the lifelong journey includes honest, continued navigation of genuine doubt, with sustained, faithful return to Scripture’s stable foundation being the ongoing, genuine goal.$gs$),
  ('d12758ba-2d39-5e7e-b7dd-538389a77b94', '9328d66a-ad45-5237-8437-e4a74d1006c2', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read 1 John 5:11-13 once more, reflecting on the complete scope of assurance explored throughout this study.
2. Write a summary of the most important lesson you learned in this entire plan.
3. Identify one specific practice from this plan you will commit to as a lifelong habit.
4. Share your growth with your peer guide, along with continued areas for growth and confidence.
5. Write a closing prayer committing to a lifetime of settled, genuine confidence in your salvation in every season ahead.$gs$)
on conflict (id) do nothing;
