-- Book 6 · Lesson 2.3: Baptism as Identification With Christ’s Body
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('655d677f-dce7-5f9e-a639-ddc9335a893d', '1b3515d6-130c-5553-b152-213bf7ea3bf3', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$Why does Paul’s specific description — baptism into genuine “one body” — reveal that this act identifies a believer not only with Christ personally, but also with His broader, corporate church throughout this significant, comprehensive act of identification?

Paul’s specific description reveals identification with the broader church, since baptism into genuine “one body” establishes this corporate, comprehensive identification, meaning this act identifies believers not only with Christ personally but also with His broader church, but this passage’s specific description particularly requiring recognition of this corporate dimension as characteristic of baptism’s genuine, comprehensive significance throughout believers’ understanding of their identification with both Christ and His broader, gathered people.$gs$),
  ('cd4f55fc-ee0e-5db2-b87d-fd6f27661bd4', '1b3515d6-130c-5553-b152-213bf7ea3bf3', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$How does this corporate dimension provide important motivation for pursuing baptism within genuine, local church community, rather than treating this significant step as merely private, individual transaction disconnected from this passage’s called-for, corporate identification and belonging?

This corporate dimension provides important motivation for pursuing this within community, since corporate identification differs from private, individual transaction, meaning believers should pursue baptism within genuine, local church community, not treating this as merely private matter, but understanding this passage’s called-for, corporate dimension as meaningful reason for pursuing baptism within their own, genuine local church community and continued belonging throughout their ongoing, church-connected life and faith.$gs$),
  ('545b0e32-ee5a-5ef0-aa0f-d90c94fca4f1', '1b3515d6-130c-5553-b152-213bf7ea3bf3', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Emphasizing this corporate dimension does not mean baptism’s meaning depends on the size or particular circumstances of the gathering; it means genuine connection to Christ’s broader church, however this specifically manifests, represents meaningful, important dimension of baptism’s comprehensive significance.$gs$),
  ('57cce4f0-603e-5c66-9ce7-dad8d2285eab', '1b3515d6-130c-5553-b152-213bf7ea3bf3', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read 1 Corinthians 12:12-13 and reflect on baptism’s corporate identification with Christ’s body.
2. If you have not yet been baptized, discuss pursuing this within your local church community this week.
3. If you have been baptized, reflect on how that experience connected you to your church community.
4. Discuss with your peer guide how pursuing baptism within community shaped their own experience.
5. Journal about your own, growing appreciation for this corporate dimension of baptism’s significance.$gs$)
