-- Book 6 · Lesson 4.2: Remembering Your Baptism in Times of Temptation
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('7f23c2db-e284-5b50-9d0a-d5e2aecddb05', '6650ff12-2106-5dc0-a7db-056dd1b4b19a', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$Why does Paul’s specific teaching — the “old man” genuinely “crucified” — provide practical resource for believers facing temptation, reminding them of a genuine, accomplished reality rather than leaving them to fight temptation through willpower alone?

Paul’s specific teaching provides practical resource for facing temptation, since the “old man” genuinely “crucified” reminds believers of an accomplished reality, meaning believers facing temptation can draw on this genuine, accomplished truth, not fighting through willpower alone, but this passage’s specific teaching particularly providing this practical, remembered resource as characteristic of genuine, biblical strategy throughout believers’ ongoing battle with temptation and continued reliance on this pictured, accomplished reality.$gs$),
  ('05856bdb-8812-539d-b3c2-622a6eb3e834', '6650ff12-2106-5dc0-a7db-056dd1b4b19a', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$How might believers develop the practical habit of specifically remembering their baptism — this pictured death to the old life — during moments of genuine temptation, using this concrete memory as reminder of who they genuinely, now are in Christ?

Believers might develop this practical habit of remembering baptism during temptation, since concrete memory provides reminder of genuine, new identity, meaning believers should develop this specific, practical habit, using this concrete memory as reminder during genuine temptation, not relying on abstract willpower alone, but drawing on this passage’s pictured, accomplished reality throughout their ongoing, practical battle against temptation and continued reliance on their genuine, new identity in Christ.$gs$),
  ('10946b79-a46d-58a1-9d23-f37fba99fa4d', '6650ff12-2106-5dc0-a7db-056dd1b4b19a', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Remembering baptism during temptation does not function as magical formula automatically preventing sin; it provides genuine, truthful reminder of identity and accomplished reality that supports, alongside other spiritual disciplines, believers’ ongoing resistance to temptation.$gs$),
  ('3f78bca4-e9b4-55e8-b10c-d3df2ed2d5b4', '6650ff12-2106-5dc0-a7db-056dd1b4b19a', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Romans 6:6-11 and reflect on the old self genuinely crucified as practical resource against temptation.
2. Identify a current temptation where you could draw on this specific, accomplished truth.
3. Practice remembering your baptism intentionally the next time you face this temptation this week.
4. Discuss with your peer guide how they draw on their own baptism during moments of genuine temptation.
5. Journal about your own, developing practice of remembering this truth throughout your ongoing struggle.$gs$)
