-- Book 6 · Lesson 4.3: A Lifetime Shaped by This Identification
insert into public.p2p_lesson_sections (id, lesson_id, section_order, section_type, title, content) values
  ('7275b336-6fe4-5559-8ce8-82129297022f', 'e5dbb24a-1245-5208-bfb2-070231ae2589', 3, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 1$gs$, $gs$What is the ultimate posture believers are meant to carry throughout their entire lives regarding this significant, biblical understanding of baptism and identification with Christ?

A sustained, lifelong commitment to understanding baptism’s genuine meaning as public declaration and vivid picture, following Scripture’s consistent pattern, approaching this step with genuine privilege and courage, and continuing to walk in the newness of life this baptism pictures throughout every season of ongoing faith, obedience, and continued discipleship.$gs$),
  ('6f070a38-8055-5bd6-820c-6ca1ea44aaf8', 'e5dbb24a-1245-5208-bfb2-070231ae2589', 4, 'teaching', $gs$Study question 2$gs$, $gs$Why must this identification remain an ongoing, lifelong posture rather than a single, completed event set aside without continued, daily application throughout believers’ ongoing spiritual life?

Because the reality baptism pictures — death to the old life, resurrection to the new — requires continued, daily expression throughout every season of ongoing life, this identification necessarily requires continued, deliberate application throughout an entire lifetime, not a single event set aside once completed, but requiring this ongoing, daily walking throughout believers’ entire, continuing faith and relationship with Christ.$gs$),
  ('7c8c8763-f0af-5793-b2ae-6c88371f1a77', 'e5dbb24a-1245-5208-bfb2-070231ae2589', 5, 'teaching', $gs$Important Distinction$gs$, $gs$Committing to this lifelong posture does not mean every day will feel equally victorious or transformed; the lifelong journey includes continued growth and struggle, with sustained, faithful walking in this pictured, new-life reality being the genuine, ongoing goal.$gs$),
  ('e331ecd3-1970-5d67-9e94-9fb7925bd419', 'e5dbb24a-1245-5208-bfb2-070231ae2589', 7, 'teaching', $gs$Lesson Assignment$gs$, $gs$1. Read Romans 6:1-11 once more, reflecting on the complete scope of baptism’s meaning explored throughout this study.
2. Write a summary of the most important lesson you learned in this entire plan.
3. Identify one specific practice from this plan you will commit to as a lifelong habit.
4. Share your growth with your peer guide, along with continued areas for growth and faithfulness.
5. Write a closing prayer committing to a lifetime of walking in the newness of life your baptism pictures.$gs$)
