  ('f60fd307-d80e-5d07-93ca-333f0eb71f68', 'ca6741b0-ce37-5e3e-869f-b31a9dbe145e', 'paragraph', $gs${"text":"Study question 1\n\nWhy does Jesus’s specific condition — genuinely “abiding” in His word — reveal that discipleship involves ongoing, continued learning and following, not remaining confined to a single, past moment of initial belief alone?\n\nJesus’s specific condition reveals discipleship’s requirement for ongoing learning, since genuinely “abiding” in His word establishes this continued, not past-moment-alone, practice, meaning discipleship involves this ongoing, continued learning and following, not a single, past moment, but this passage’s specific condition particularly requiring recognition of this continued, ongoing abiding as characteristic of genuine, biblical discipleship throughout believers’ entire, continuing life and relationship with Christ’s word and teaching."}$gs$::jsonb, 6, false, false),
