  ('de3c20e3-345e-56b8-ba1e-1457e53a9ea5', 'bf8d8cdd-9c1a-52fd-8aa4-9c996529155e', 'paragraph', $gs${"text":"Study question 2\n\nHow does actively seeking out this kind of mentoring relationship — someone genuinely further along, willing to walk personally alongside — provide practical guidance and encouragement that solitary reading and prayer, however genuinely valuable, cannot fully replace during ongoing growth?\n\nActively seeking mentoring provides practical guidance solitary practice cannot fully replace, since personal walking-alongside differs from solitary reading and prayer alone, meaning believers should actively seek this mentoring relationship, not relying exclusively on solitary practice, but pursuing this passage’s modeled, personal relationship throughout their ongoing, continued growth and development as maturing, growing disciples of Christ."}$gs$::jsonb, 4, false, false),
